  "intro": "Arabic has two words for 'uncle' and two for 'aunt'. Your father's brother is عَمّ and his sister is عَمَّة; your mother's brother is خَال and her sister is خَالَة. Cousins are named through them: اِبْنُ عَمِّي is 'the son of my uncle'. In such a chain only the last word takes 'my'.",
